Day 24: Prompts in LangChain

Temperature recap:
Temperature controls creativity.
Write a poem with temperature 0: same output every time for the same input.
Raise temperature: output can change even when the input stays the same.

What are prompts:
Prompts are the input instructions or query given to a model to guide the output.

Types of prompts (by content):
1. Text based prompts: only text.
2. Multimodal prompts: text plus image, sound, or video.
Main focus: text based prompts. Used about 99% of the time.
Prompts are so important that prompt engineering is its own job profile.

Static vs dynamic prompts:
What we were doing: model.invoke("whats the capital of nepal")
In real life the user types the prompt and clicks send. The LLM receives it and replies.
As a developer we do not hard write every prompt by hand for each user.

f strings vs PromptTemplate:
You can use f strings, but PromptTemplate is better.
You get options like validate_template=True.
You can reuse the template many times.
You can save a template to a file such as template.json.

